  "subtitle-win": [
    "France and Spain lead the 2026 World Cup winner market with closely matched implied probabilities, reflecting their status as the top two sides in recent FIFA rankings and power assessments. Spain enters as European champions with an extended unbeaten run in competitive fixtures, while France benefits from exceptional squad depth and consistent results in recent Nations League and qualifying campaigns. England, Argentina, Portugal, and Brazil follow tightly behind due to strong recent form, experienced cores, and favorable group draws in the expanded 48-team field. This bunched pricing underscores the parity among elite European and South American contenders, where minor shifts in fitness, tactical execution, or knockout matchups could readily alter the hierarchy before the July final."
